a week after 11 years?

00:10:49.738 --> 00:10:51.170
Why do you guys think I
go out seven nights a week

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.236
after 11 years?

00:10:52.236 --> 00:10:53.462
- [Answerer] To be good at what you do.

00:10:53.462 --> 00:10:57.062
- 'Cause I appreciate that
I'm in the position I'm in.

00:10:57.062 --> 00:10:59.765
I say it's a privilege, it's a privilege.

00:10:59.765 --> 00:11:01.571
This is not some entitle.

00:11:01.571 --> 00:11:04.032
That's a privilege to be in that position.

00:11:04.032 --> 00:11:05.339
I've got a big audience here

00:11:05.339 --> 00:11:07.548
to listen to what I
have to say about life,

00:11:07.548 --> 00:11:10.346
success with women, success.

00:11:10.346 --> 00:11:13.580
That's a privilege so I
take that very seriously

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:16.769
and I think that success
is something that is earned

00:11:16.769 --> 00:11:18.735
and re-earned.

00:11:18.735 --> 00:11:21.845
I think that in life, you're
climbing up that mountain

00:11:21.845 --> 00:11:24.351
and you want to take breaks strategically

00:11:24.351 --> 00:11:26.645
but people think that you
can climb up a mountain

00:11:26.645 --> 00:11:28.083
and just kind of stay there.

00:11:28.083 --> 00:11:30.825
Not really, I view it like
it's like a muddy mountain.

00:11:30.825 --> 00:11:33.322
You climb up and you stay there.

00:11:33.322 --> 00:11:35.087
You start to slide down

00:11:35.087 --> 00:11:37.009
and there's a number of
reasons why that happens.

00:11:37.009 --> 00:11:38.756
I'll talk about them today.

00:11:38.756 --> 00:11:40.633
Does that mean you should
never take a break?

00:11:40.633 --> 00:11:41.908
No.

00:11:41.908 --> 00:11:43.074
I'm going to take a little time off

00:11:43.074 --> 00:11:46.391
when I do my Miami events this year.

00:11:46.391 --> 00:11:48.976
I'm going to sit there
eating sushi in South Beach

00:11:48.976 --> 00:11:51.915
and stare at my belly button

00:11:51.915 --> 00:11:54.265
and I'm just going to be great, okay?

00:11:54.265 --> 00:11:56.557
And I'm looking forward to going out

00:11:56.557 --> 00:11:58.314
to the islands in Hawaii this summer

00:11:58.314 --> 00:11:59.337
and that's a long ways off

00:11:59.337 --> 00:12:01.586
but when I'm suffering
hard with the workload,

00:12:01.586 --> 00:12:02.811
that's something I can look forward to

00:12:02.811 --> 00:12:05.064
and I'm going to sit beside a waterfall

00:12:05.064 --> 00:12:06.374
and I'm going to sit there convulsing

00:12:06.374 --> 00:12:08.420
while my body flushes the
year's worth of quarters

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:09.694
all out of it.

00:12:09.694 --> 00:12:12.720
That's basically what I do.

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:14.273
Cool.

00:12:14.273 --> 00:12:15.742
Of course I believe in taking a break.

00:12:15.742 --> 00:12:18.195
I think you should spend time
with friends and take breaks

00:12:18.195 --> 00:12:19.462
but I also believe that success

00:12:19.462 --> 00:12:24.042
is something that has to
be earned and re-earned.

00:12:24.042 --> 00:12:25.840
The world is a dynamic place.

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:27.150
The world is changing.

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:28.789
If you're not changing along with it,

00:12:28.789 --> 00:12:30.752
you're probably being left behind.

00:12:30.752 --> 00:12:33.210
It's so crazy how as an entrepreneur

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.518
or as somebody even who in their career

00:12:34.518 --> 00:12:36.058
wants to be at a high level,

00:12:36.058 --> 00:12:39.388
you have to like boundary
off so many behaviors

00:12:39.388 --> 00:12:41.636
and influences that other people let in.

00:12:41.636 --> 00:12:43.273
So essentially somebody at a high level,

00:12:43.273 --> 00:12:44.705
they've just made the choice to say, hey,

00:12:44.705 --> 00:12:46.342
if there's somebody who's overly dramatic

00:12:46.342 --> 00:12:49.039
or disruptive in my life,
maybe you have to let them go.

00:12:49.039 --> 00:12:50.484
It's super sad.

00:12:50.484 --> 00:12:52.697
And if there's foods that are depleting me

00:12:52.697 --> 00:12:54.172
or habits that are depleting me

00:12:54.172 --> 00:12:56.626
or things that are making
me late or not on point

00:12:56.626 --> 00:12:59.489
or not have my life together,
I have to let those go

00:12:59.489 --> 00:13:01.739
and essentially, so a lot of
it is creating those boundaries

00:13:01.739 --> 00:13:03.481
and what's funny then
is people who are maybe

00:13:03.481 --> 00:13:04.314
not quite at that level,

00:13:04.314 --> 00:13:06.138
they wish they could hang
out with people at that level

00:13:06.138 --> 00:13:07.524
but they don't realize this like

00:13:07.524 --> 00:13:09.140
it's not that that person's at

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.908
a so called higher level than you.

00:13:10.908 --> 00:13:12.399
They just have stronger boundaries

00:13:12.399 --> 00:13:13.911
and if somebody with less boundaries

00:13:13.911 --> 00:13:15.591
is coming into that
circle, it's like, hey,

00:13:15.591 --> 00:13:16.424
we'd love to have you here

00:13:16.424 --> 00:13:18.212
but just work on your
boundaries a little bit

00:13:18.212 --> 00:13:19.806
and we'd love to have you here, right?

00:13:19.806 --> 00:13:21.444
So it's like people think that

00:13:21.444 --> 00:13:23.245
other people are holding them down

00:13:23.245 --> 00:13:24.311
but really actually, a lot of the time

00:13:24.311 --> 00:13:25.374
I think they kind of feel bad for them

00:13:25.374 --> 00:13:26.743
and hope they can do better.

00:13:26.743 --> 00:13:27.644
Everybody who's at the top

00:13:27.644 --> 00:13:29.113
is hoping to see other people come up

00:13:29.113 --> 00:13:31.652
so there can be more cool
people to kick it with.

00:13:31.652 --> 00:13:33.876
I actually chose to end off this video

00:13:33.876 --> 00:13:36.535
pointing out the very
tall Rockefeller Center

00:13:36.535 --> 00:13:37.565
to make the point about how

00:13:37.565 --> 00:13:39.323
when you start to develop yourself,

00:13:39.323 --> 00:13:42.025
it can oftentimes make you
feel even more insecure.

00:13:42.025 --> 00:13:43.172
Alright, so lot of time,

00:13:43.172 --> 00:13:44.886
I'll bring a friend of mine to the gym

00:13:44.886 --> 00:13:47.056
and let's say it's a girl,
I'll bring her out to the gym

00:13:47.056 --> 00:13:49.471
and she already feels
really hot about herself

00:13:49.471 --> 00:13:50.495
but as she goes to the gym,

00:13:50.495 --> 00:13:52.167
she begins to see her weak spots.

00:13:52.167 --> 00:13:54.622
She begins to actually
realize how far she has to go

00:13:54.622 --> 00:13:55.972
and paradoxically,

00:13:55.972 --> 00:13:58.778
the very act of actually improving herself

00:13:58.778 --> 00:14:02.288
makes her feel even more insecure.

00:14:02.288 --> 00:14:03.123
You'll see the same thing when guys

00:14:03.123 --> 00:14:05.743
actually try to get a
little bit of money going

00:14:05.743 --> 00:14:06.645
or let's say that they try to learn

00:14:06.645 --> 00:14:07.709
to be good with girls, right?

00:14:07.709 --> 00:14:09.631
Let's say you actually
thought your money was okay

00:14:09.631 --> 00:14:12.291
and then you start improving
your cash situation.

00:14:12.291 --> 00:14:13.150
All of a sudden, you realize,

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:14.681
damn, if I want to get
a good business going

00:14:14.681 --> 00:14:16.808
or I want to get my career
going with some good momentum,

00:14:16.808 --> 00:14:18.774
I have a lot further
to go than I realized.

00:14:18.774 --> 00:14:20.289
Likewise, as far as girls go,

00:14:20.289 --> 00:14:22.006
most guys actually walk
around thinking like,

00:14:22.006 --> 00:14:24.545
they could win any fight,
they could pick up any girl

00:14:24.545 --> 00:14:25.650
but when you actually go and try to do it

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.166
and you realize how much you suck,

00:14:27.166 --> 00:14:28.931
it winds up making you
feel even more insecure.

00:14:28.931 --> 00:14:31.463
So just remember that the fact

00:14:31.463 --> 00:14:33.386
that you are trying to improve yourself,

00:14:33.386 --> 00:14:36.127
it's a paradox between
self-improvement and self-acceptance

00:14:36.127 --> 00:14:38.717
because the very act of improving yourself

00:14:38.717 --> 00:14:40.559
sometimes can make you
feel a little bit bad.

00:14:40.559 --> 00:14:41.867
What's the frame that I come from then?

00:14:41.867 --> 00:14:43.789
How do I do all the self-improvement stuff

00:14:43.789 --> 00:14:45.471
and not feel terrible?

00:14:45.471 --> 00:14:48.605
Well, what I do is I
come from a basic frame

00:14:48.605 --> 00:14:51.434
and the basic frame is I'm already awesome

00:14:51.434 --> 00:14:53.601
and I'm just enjoying my journey

00:14:53.601 --> 00:14:56.052
of becoming even more awesome.

00:14:56.052 --> 00:14:58.221
So I remember back when I
was first teaching bootcamps,

00:14:58.221 --> 00:14:59.121
one of the first ones I ever taught

00:14:59.121 --> 00:15:00.716
was here in New York City.

00:15:00.716 --> 00:15:01.699
I didn't really have a lot of students.

00:15:01.699 --> 00:15:03.089
We didn't charge a lot of money

00:15:03.089 --> 00:15:04.560
and I probably wasn't the best teacher

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:06.523
so you might not have want
to be at that bootcamp

00:15:06.523 --> 00:15:07.913
but the point being

00:15:07.913 --> 00:15:11.802
was I was teaching
bootcamp in a Starbucks.

00:15:11.802 --> 00:15:16.315
I'd sneak into an HIV clinic
and say that I had HIV

00:15:16.315 --> 00:15:17.752
or we'd break into a school building

00:15:17.752 --> 00:15:18.998
and do it on milk crates.

00:15:18.998 --> 00:15:21.052
I'd be doing seminars
in those environments

00:15:21.052 --> 00:15:22.115
and if you would have asked me

00:15:22.115 --> 00:15:23.550
if I thought what I was doing was cool,

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:24.983
I'd say yeah, it's cool.

00:15:24.983 --> 00:15:27.356
Right now, I might teach a
four or 500 person seminar

00:15:27.356 --> 00:15:28.583
at a hotel.

00:15:28.583 --> 00:15:29.976
You ask me if I think it's cool.

00:15:29.976 --> 00:15:31.368
I say I think it's cool.

00:15:31.368 --> 00:15:33.988
Someday, I could be teaching
a 5000 person audience

00:15:33.988 --> 00:15:35.220
in a big auditorium somewhere

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:38.083
like some kind of convention center

00:15:38.083 --> 00:15:40.878
and if you ask me if I think
it's cool, I think that's cool.

00:15:40.878 --> 00:15:42.188
And if I was to run the whole damn planet,

00:15:42.188 --> 00:15:43.659
I'll think that's cool too.

00:15:43.659 --> 00:15:46.809
Wherever I am on my journey,
I'm loving it, okay?

00:15:46.809 --> 00:15:49.801
I love the journey because
as far as I'm concerned,

00:15:49.801 --> 00:15:52.133
the golden era is now.

00:15:52.133 --> 00:15:55.035
The golden era is the present moment

00:15:55.035 --> 00:15:58.180
and wherever I am, right,
if you're asking me now,

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.167
oh, did it suck when you taught

00:15:59.167 --> 00:16:00.762
the programs back at Starbucks?

00:16:00.762 --> 00:16:02.194
No, it was awesome.

00:16:02.194 --> 00:16:04.162
I was already awesome
and enjoying my journey

00:16:04.162 --> 00:16:05.544
to become even more awesome, right?

00:16:05.544 --> 00:16:07.102
And someday, if I'm teaching 5000 people,

00:16:07.102 --> 00:16:08.699
you say, oh teaching 500 people,

00:16:08.699 --> 00:16:10.009
was that too small of a crowd for you?

00:16:10.009 --> 00:16:12.261
I'd say no, I was just
enjoying my journey.

00:16:12.261 --> 00:16:14.385
I was awesome, I'm just
enjoying being on the path

00:16:14.385 --> 00:16:16.674
to becoming even more awesome.

00:16:16.674 --> 00:16:19.093
I understand that cultures
brainwash you all the time

00:16:19.093 --> 00:16:20.760
to desire completion

00:16:21.839 --> 00:16:25.406
and this could be a 10 hour
seminar on this one topic,

00:16:25.406 --> 00:16:29.454
how, literally how society
brainwashes you to think

00:16:29.454 --> 00:16:31.954
that there will be completion.

00:16:32.859 --> 00:16:34.455
Yeah, there's no one trying to control you

00:16:34.455 --> 00:16:36.421
but just the way that society works out,

00:16:36.421 --> 00:16:37.797
again, it's trying to be like,

00:16:37.797 --> 00:16:39.268
